// each struct/map item has its own optional trailing comma, distinct from
// the comma separating it from the next item -- two commas in a row are
// legal, and a struct's/map's own trailing comma (after its closing
// bracket) is what lets two top-level values sit side by side
(a: 1,, b: 2)
{x: 1,, y: 2}
(first: 1),
(second: 2)
{third: 1},
{fourth: 2}
[(a: 1),, (b: 2)]
